function navItem(id,label){const r=currentRoute().split('/')[0];const current=r===id||(id==='book'&&(r==='module'||r==='lesson'))||(id==='software'&&r==='guide');return `<button class="nav-item ${current?'active':''}" data-route="${id}"><span class="nav-icon">${icons[id]}</span>${label}</button>`}
function frame(content){let route=currentRoute(),title=route.split('/')[0];const m=getModule(route.split('/')[1]);return `<a class="skip-link" href="#main-content" data-action="skip-main">Skip to learning content</a><div class="app-shell"><aside class="sidebar ${state.navOpen?'open':''}"><a class="brand" href="#dashboard" data-route="dashboard"><span class="brand-mark">F</span><span class="brand-word">FabReady<small>SOFTWARE & AI ACADEMY</small></span></a><div class="nav-heading">LEARNING SPACE</div>${navItem('dashboard','My dashboard')}${navItem('coding','Zero-to-pro coding')}${navItem('book','Digital textbook')}${navItem('pro','NT$100k+ career track')}${navItem('workspace','Developer Studio')}${navItem('labs','Live coding labs')}${navItem('practice','Practice & exams')}${navItem('software','Software walkthroughs')}<div class="nav-heading">GET HIRED</div>${navItem('portfolio','Portfolio projects')}${navItem('interview','Senior interview simulator')}${navItem('career','Kaohsiung career hub')}${navItem('glossary','Mandarin glossary')}<div class="sidebar-bottom"><div class="space-between"><span style="font-size:12px;font-weight:800">Learning progress</span><b style="font-size:11px;color:var(--accent)">${percent(countDone(),LESSONS.length)}%</b></div><div class="mini-progress"><span style="width:${percent(countDone(),LESSONS.length)}%"></span></div><p>${countDone()} of ${LESSONS.length} lessons finished<br>Stored privately in this browser.</p><button class="btn btn-ghost" style="width:100%;margin-top:9px" data-action="export-progress">↓ Export progress</button><button class="btn btn-ghost" style="width:100%;margin-top:4px" data-action="restore-progress">↑ Restore progress</button><input type="file" id="progress-import" accept=".json,application/json" hidden></div></aside><main class="main" id="main-content" tabindex="-1"><header class="topbar"><div class="topbar-left"><button class="mobile-menu" data-action="menu" aria-label="Toggle navigation" aria-expanded="${state.navOpen}">☰</button><span>FabReady Academy</span><span class="crumb-dot">/</span><b>${esc(m?.name||routeLabels[title]||'Dashboard')}</b></div><div class="topbar-right"><div class="search-shell"><span class="search-ico">⌕</span><input id="global-search" placeholder="Find lessons, software..." aria-label="Search lessons and software" /></div><span class="tiny-pill">KAOHSIUNG · TAIWAN</span><span class="avatar">AI</span></div></header><div class="page">${content}</div></main></div>`}
const routeLabels={workspace:'Developer Studio',coding:'Coding academy',dashboard:'Dashboard',book:'Textbook',pro:'Professional track',interview:'Interview simulator',module:'Chapter',lesson:'Lesson',labs:'Labs',practice:'Practice',software:'Software',guide:'Guide',portfolio:'Portfolio',project:'Capstone brief',career:'Career',glossary:'Glossary',search:'Search results'};
function waferVisual(){let s='<div class="hero-graphic"><div class="wafer-orbit"></div><div class="wafer">';for(let i=0;i<144;i++){let x=i%12,y=Math.floor(i/12),cls=(x>=8&&y>=4&&y<=7)||(x===6&&y===3)?'hot':(x>=3&&x<=6&&y>=3&&y<=7)?'warn':'';s+=`<span class="die ${cls}"></span>`}return s+'</div><div class="wafer-label">PATTERN DETECTED // 08</div></div>'}
function stats(){return `<div class="stat-grid"><div class="stat-card"><div class="label">Textbook lessons</div><div class="value">${LESSONS.length}</div><div class="desc">Across ${MODULES.length} learning modules</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="label">Lessons completed</div><div class="value">${countDone()}<span style="font-size:14px;color:var(--muted)"> / ${LESSONS.length}</span></div><div class="desc">Complete each after practicing</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="label">Knowledge checks passed</div><div class="value">${quizDone()}</div><div class="desc">Verified multiple-choice answers</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="label">Coding challenges passed</div><div class="value">${labDone()}<span style="font-size:14px;color:var(--muted)"> / ${sqlTasks.length+pyTasks.length+CODING_DRILLS.length}</span></div><div class="desc">SQL, Python & JavaScript</div></div></div>`}
function moduleCard(m){const a=mLessons(m.id),done=a.filter(l=>state.completed[l.id]).length;return `<div class="module-card" style="--module-color:${m.color}" role="button" tabindex="0" data-route="module/${m.id}"><div class="module-top"><span class="module-symbol">${String(MODULES.indexOf(m)).padStart(2,'0')}</span><span class="module-count">${a.length} LESSONS · ${m.level.toUpperCase()}</span></div><h3>${esc(m.name.replace(/^\d+ · /,''))}</h3><p>${esc(m.description)}</p><div class="module-foot"><span>${done}/${a.length} completed</span><span>Explore →</span></div><div class="module-progress"><i style="width:${percent(done,a.length)}%"></i></div></div>`}
function dashboard(){let next=LESSONS.find(l=>!state.completed[l.id])||LESSONS[0];return `<div class="hero"><div class="hero-copy"><div class="hero-pills"><span class="small-outline">ZERO → ADVANCED</span><span class="small-outline">ABOVE NT$100k MONTHLY BASE TARGET</span></div><h1>From beginner to<br><em>professional software engineer.</em></h1><p>A rigorous, practical learning program for senior-track AI, data and software careers. Built for a strict NT$100,000+ fixed monthly base-salary goal in Kaohsiung—not a salary guarantee.</p><div class="hero-actions"><button class="btn btn-primary" data-route="coding">Start zero-to-pro coding ↗</button><button class="btn btn-secondary" data-route="workspace">Open coding workspace ↗</button><button class="btn btn-secondary" data-route="pro">View my NT$100k track ↗</button></div></div>${waferVisual()}</div>${stats()}<div class="salary-strip"><div><span class="section-kicker">YOUR NON-NEGOTIABLE TARGET</span><h2>NT$100,000+ <small>fixed monthly base · Kaohsiung</small></h2><p>Bonus, profit sharing, stock, overtime and allowances do not count. Build technical evidence and confirm each offer's written base.</p></div><button class="btn btn-secondary" data-route="pro">Open professional track →</button></div><div class="section-head"><h2>Your next step</h2><button class="minor-link" data-route="practice">Practice exam →</button></div><button class="chapter-row" data-route="lesson/${next.id}"><span class="chapter-num">▶</span><span><h3>${esc(next.title)}</h3><p>${esc(getModule(next.module).name)} · ${next.minutes} minute estimated reading and practice</p></span><span class="chapter-side">Open ↗</span></button><div class="section-head"><h2>The complete learning path</h2><button class="minor-link" data-route="book">View all chapters →</button></div><div class="module-grid">${MODULES.map(moduleCard).join('')}</div><p class="footnote">FabReady targets more than NT$100,000 fixed monthly base pay, not bonus-inclusive compensation. It measures study activity, not professional rank or offer probability. Strong job preparation also requires independently built projects, interviews, relevant vacancies and language fit.</p>`}
function book(){let filter=state.filter;let mods=MODULES.filter(m=>filter==='All'||m.level===filter);return `<div class="section-kicker">THE DIGITAL TEXTBOOK</div><h1 class="page-title">A serious roadmap from zero to deployment.</h1><p class="page-description">${LESSONS.length} original lessons, ${MODULES.length} progressive modules, guided explanations, worked examples, pitfalls, exercises and knowledge checks. Includes computer science, software engineering, industrial AI and cross-industry applications.</p><div class="category-strip">${['All','Starter','Intermediate','Advanced','Expert','Career'].map(x=>`<button class="filter-btn ${filter===x?'active':''}" data-filter="${esc(x)}">${x}</button>`).join('')}</div><div class="module-grid">${mods.map(moduleCard).join('')}</div>`}
function moduleView(id){let m=getModule(id);if(!m)return notFound();let ls=mLessons(id),done=ls.filter(l=>state.completed[l.id]).length;return `<div class="reader-header"><button class="back-link" data-route="book">← All textbook modules</button><span class="chapter-tag">${esc(m.level)}</span></div><div class="section-kicker">${esc(m.area.toUpperCase())} · ${ls.length} LESSONS</div><h1 class="page-title">${esc(m.name)}</h1><p class="page-description">${esc(m.description)} Complete the reading, do the practice and pass the knowledge check before moving to the next chapter.</p><div class="notice">Progress: ${done}/${ls.length} lessons complete. <strong>${percent(done,ls.length)}%</strong> of this module done. Completion is self-attested; quiz results are separately verified.</div><div class="section-head"><h2>Lessons in this chapter</h2><span class="muted" style="font-size:12px">Estimated ${ls.reduce((a,l)=>a+l.minutes,0)} minutes + labs</span></div><div class="chapter-list">${ls.map((l,i)=>`<button class="chapter-row ${state.completed[l.id]?'completed':''}" data-route="lesson/${l.id}"><span class="chapter-num">${state.completed[l.id]?'✓':String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><span><h3>${esc(l.title)}</h3><p>${esc(l.objective)}</p></span><span class="chapter-side">${l.minutes} min <span>→</span></span></button>`).join('')}</div><div class="section-head"><h2>Keep practicing</h2></div><div class="notice">Each lesson has an individual worked example, an exercise and a quiz. For executable practice use the <button class="minor-link" data-route="labs">SQL / Python labs ↗</button>. For software setup use <button class="minor-link" data-route="software">step-by-step tool guides ↗</button>.</div>`}
function lessonView(id){const l=getLesson(id);if(!l)return notFound();const m=getModule(l.module),idx=lessonIndex(id),next=LESSONS[idx+1],prev=LESSONS[idx-1],quiz=l.quiz,qs=state.lessonSelected;return `<div class="reader-header"><button class="back-link" data-route="module/${l.module}">← ${esc(m.name)}</button><span class="chapter-tag">${esc(m.level)} · ${l.minutes} min</span></div><div class="two-col"><div class="book-content"><div class="section-kicker">CHAPTER ${String(MODULES.indexOf(m)).padStart(2,'0')} / LESSON ${mLessons(l.module).indexOf(l)+1}</div><h1 class="reader-headline">${esc(l.title)}</h1><div class="reader-meta"><span>◷ ${l.minutes} min reading & activity</span><span>◎ ${esc(m.area)}</span><span>${state.quizzes[id]?'✓ Check passed':'○ Check not passed'}</span></div><div class="content-panel"><h2>What you will understand</h2><div class="prose">${paragraphs(l.objective)}</div><div class="divider"></div><h2>The theory, explained</h2><div class="prose">${paragraphs(l.theory)}</div></div><div class="content-panel"><h2>Worked example</h2><div class="prose">${paragraphs(l.example)}</div>${l.code?`<div class="mt"><div class="code-caption">EXAMPLE CODE ${l.type==='sql'?'· SQL':'· CODE'}</div><div class="code-box">${esc(l.code)}</div><div class="row mt"><button class="btn btn-ghost" data-action="copy-code" data-id="${l.id}">Copy example</button>${l.type==='sql'?`<button class="btn btn-secondary" data-action="lab-from-lesson" data-id="${l.id}">Try in SQL lab ↗</button>`:''}</div></div>`:''}<div class="callout warn"><div class="callout-title">⚠ COMMON MISTAKE</div><p>${esc(l.pitfall)}</p></div></div><div class="practice-box"><div class="section-kicker">YOUR TURN · GUIDED RECALL</div><h2 class="practice-title">Apply what you just learned</h2><p class="question">${esc(l.task)}</p><textarea id="practice-draft" placeholder="Explain your reasoning, paste your query, or write the key steps...">${esc(state.lessonDraft)}</textarea><div class="row"><button class="btn btn-primary" data-action="review-draft" data-id="${l.id}">Review my reasoning</button><button class="btn btn-secondary" data-action="ask-mistake" data-id="${l.id}">Ask FabMentor ↗</button></div>${state.practiceFeedback?`<div class="feedback">${esc(state.practiceFeedback)}</div>`:''}<details class="answer-details"><summary>Reveal model reasoning (after trying)</summary><p>${esc(l.answer)}</p></details></div><div class="content-panel"><div class="section-kicker">KNOWLEDGE CHECK</div><h2>Can you explain the core idea?</h2><p class="prose">${esc(quiz.q)}</p><div class="quiz-options">${quiz.options.map((o,i)=>`<button class="quiz-option ${qs===i?'selected':''}" data-action="quiz-pick" data-index="${i}"><span class="option-letter">${'ABCD'[i]}</span>${esc(o)}</button>`).join('')}</div><div class="row"><button class="btn btn-primary" data-action="quiz-check" data-id="${l.id}" ${qs===-1?'disabled':''}>Check answer</button><span class="muted" style="font-size:11px">${state.quizzes[id]?'✓ Previously passed':''}</span></div>${state.quizFeedback?`<div class="feedback ${state.quizFeedback.startsWith('Correct')?'success':'error'}">${esc(state.quizFeedback)}</div>`:''}</div>${l.reference?`<div class="content-panel"><h2>Primary dataset / documentation</h2><p class="prose">Open the source directly to check released metadata, terms of use, and data meaning.</p><a class="reference-link" href="${esc(safeUrl(l.reference))}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View official or public reference ↗</a></div>`:''}<div class="content-panel space-between"><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" id="lesson-complete" ${state.completed[id]?'checked':''} data-action="complete" data-id="${l.id}" /> I completed this lesson and attempted its exercise.</label><button class="btn btn-secondary" data-route="${next?'lesson/'+next.id:'book'}">${next?'Next lesson →':'Back to textbook'}</button></div>${prev?`<button class="back-link" data-route="lesson/${prev.id}">← Previous: ${esc(prev.title)}</button>`:''}</div><aside class="rail">${mentorView(l)}<div class="rail-card"><h3>What matters in interviews</h3><p>${esc(l.pitfall)}</p><button class="rail-link btn btn-ghost" data-route="practice">Try the 10-question exam ↗</button></div></aside></div>`}
function mentorView(l){return `<div class="mentor-card"><div class="mentor-top"><span class="mentor-icon">✦</span><div><b>FabMentor AI</b><small>Context-aware learning coach</small></div></div><div class="mentor-body"><div class="mentor-welcome">Ask why your solution is wrong, get a hint, or request a step-by-step explanation. The tutor is grounded in this lesson's concepts and will distinguish known facts from assumptions.</div><div class="mentor-quick"><button data-action="mentor-quick" data-prompt="Explain this lesson more simply, with a fresh manufacturing example.">Explain simply</button><button data-action="mentor-quick" data-prompt="Give me one hint to solve the exercise without revealing the full answer.">One hint</button><button data-action="mentor-quick" data-prompt="Identify the first incorrect step in my attempt and explain why. If there is no attempt, ask me to paste it.">Find my mistake</button></div>${state.chat.length?`<div class="chat-scroll" id="chat-scroll">${state.chat.map(c=>`<div class="chat-msg ${c.role==='user'?'mine':''}">${esc(c.text)}</div>`).join('')}</div>`:''}<textarea id="mentor-input" class="tutor-input" placeholder="What did I do wrong with this SQL query?">${esc(state.tutorText)}</textarea><button class="btn btn-primary" style="width:100%" data-action="mentor-send" ${state.tutorBusy?'disabled':''}>${state.tutorBusy?'Thinking…':'Ask FabMentor ✦'}</button><details class="tutor-access"><summary>Optional private AI tutor access</summary><p class="mentor-note">For your personal Vercel deployment, set OPENAI_API_KEY, ENABLE_AI_TUTOR=1 and TUTOR_ACCESS_CODE on the server, then enter that private code below. Without it, a limited offline coach responds. Never submit private employer or patient data.</p><input class="input-field" type="password" id="tutor-access-code" placeholder="Private tutor access code (not saved to disk)" autocomplete="off" /></details></div></div>`}
function software(){let filters=['All',...new Set(GUIDES.map(g=>g.level))];let f=state.softwareFilter;let list=GUIDES.filter(g=>(f==='All'||g.level===f)&&(!state.guideSearch||[g.name,g.goal,g.category].join(' ').toLowerCase().includes(state.guideSearch.toLowerCase())));return `<div class="section-kicker">SOFTWARE FIELD MANUAL</div><h1 class="page-title">Learn the tools. Every important click and command.</h1><p class="page-description">${GUIDES.length} step-by-step tool guides, from Windows and VS Code to PostgreSQL, GitHub, PyTorch, Docker, FastAPI and Vercel. Each includes setup, exercises, checks and troubleshooting.</p><div class="large-search"><input id="guide-search" placeholder="Search Docker, PostgreSQL, VS Code..." value="${esc(state.guideSearch)}" /></div><div class="category-strip">${filters.map(x=>`<button class="filter-btn ${f===x?'active':''}" data-soft-filter="${esc(x)}">${esc(x)}</button>`).join('')}</div><div class="software-grid">${list.map((g,i)=>`<div class="software-card" data-route="guide/${g.id}" role="button" tabindex="0"><div class="software-icon">${['⌘','🐍','▣','◆','▤','▰','◫','◇','▦','⌁','⬡','⇄','✳','◈','▲'][GUIDES.indexOf(g)]||'◫'}</div><small>${esc(g.category)} · ${g.level}</small><h3>${esc(g.name)}</h3><p>${esc(g.goal)}</p><span class="rail-link">Read ${g.steps.length} detailed steps →</span></div>`).join('')}</div>${!list.length?'<div class="empty">No guide matches your search.</div>':''}`}
function guideView(id){let g=GUIDES.find(g=>g.id===id);if(!g)return notFound();let done=g.steps.filter((_,i)=>state.guides[g.id+':'+i]).length;return `<div class="reader-header"><button class="back-link" data-route="software">← All software manuals</button><span class="chapter-tag">${g.level}</span></div><div class="section-kicker">${esc(g.category.toUpperCase())} · HANDS-ON WALKTHROUGH</div><h1 class="page-title">${esc(g.name)}</h1><p class="page-description">${esc(g.goal)}</p><div class="two-col"><div><div class="content-panel"><h2>Before you begin</h2><p class="prose">${esc(g.requirements)}</p><div class="metric-bar mt"><span style="width:${percent(done,g.steps.length)}%"></span></div><p class="muted" style="font-size:11px;margin:10px 0 0">${done}/${g.steps.length} steps checked off</p><div class="divider"></div>${g.steps.map(([title,body],i)=>`<div class="guide-step"><span class="step-marker">${i+1}</span><div><h3>${esc(title)}</h3><div class="prose">${paragraphs(body)}</div><label class="step-check"><input type="checkbox" data-action="guide-check" data-key="${g.id+':'+i}" ${state.guides[g.id+':'+i]?'checked':''}/> I completed this step</label></div></div>`).join('')}</div><div class="content-panel"><h2>Do it yourself</h2><p class="prose">${esc(g.exercise)}</p><div class="callout"><div class="callout-title">SUCCESS CHECK</div><p>${esc(g.check)}</p></div><div class="callout warn"><div class="callout-title">IF SOMETHING GOES WRONG</div><p>${esc(g.troubleshoot)}</p></div></div></div><aside class="rail"><div class="rail-card"><h3>Official documentation</h3><p>Follow the original product documentation when versions or menus change.</p><a href="${esc(safeUrl(g.url))}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="reference-link">Open official guide ↗</a><div class="divider"></div><button class="btn btn-secondary" data-route="labs">Practice in the coding lab ↗</button></div></aside></div>`}
function labs(){let sql=state.labTab==='sql',tasks=sql?sqlTasks:pyTasks,t=tasks[state.labIndex]||tasks[0];if(state.labCode===null)state.labCode=draftGet('lab:'+state.labTab+':'+state.labIndex)??t.starter;return `<div class="section-kicker">HANDS-ON WORKBENCH</div><h1 class="page-title">Practice real code. Get exact feedback.</h1><p class="page-description">SQL runs in an isolated, in-browser SQLite database with synthetic manufacturing tables. Python runs in an isolated browser-based Pyodide environment. No account required. Basic outputs are checked against expected results; advanced Python functions run multiple embedded assertions. These are practice checks, not independent certifications.</p><div class="lab-tabs"><button class="${sql?'active':''}" data-lab-tab="sql" ${state.labBusy?'disabled':''}>SQL factory sandbox</button><button class="${sql?'':'active'}" data-lab-tab="python" ${state.labBusy?'disabled':''}>Python practice runner</button></div><div class="lab-shell"><div class="lab-panel"><h3>${sql?'SQL CHALLENGES':'PYTHON CHALLENGES'}</h3>${tasks.map((x,i)=>`<button class="lab-challenge ${state.labIndex===i?'active':''}" data-lab-index="${i}" ${state.labBusy?'disabled':''}>${esc(x.title)} <small>${x.level} · ${state.labs[(sql?'sql':'python')+':'+i]?'✓ Passed':'Not yet passed'}</small></button>`).join('')}</div><div class="lab-main"><div class="lab-panel"><div class="section-kicker">${esc(t.level.toUpperCase())}</div><h2 style="font-family:'Space Grotesk';font-size:21px;margin:0 0 11px">${esc(t.title)}</h2><p class="prose">${esc(t.prompt)}</p>${sql?`<div class="callout"><div class="callout-title">SYNTHETIC DATABASE</div><p>lots(lot_id,product,started_at) · wafers(wafer_id,lot_id,tool_id,passed,tested,completed_at) · tools(tool_id,tool_family,area) · sensor_logs(event_id,tool_id,wafer_id,event_time,pressure,temperature,recipe)</p></div>`:''}<div class="space-between mt"><div class="code-caption">${sql?'SQLITE SQL':'PYTHON 3'} EDITOR</div><button class="minor-link" data-action="reset-code">Reset example</button></div><textarea class="code-editor" id="lab-code" spellcheck="false" aria-label="Coding editor" ${state.labBusy?'disabled':''}>
${esc(state.labCode)}</textarea><div class="row mt"><button class="btn btn-primary" data-action="run-lab" ${state.labBusy?'disabled':''}>${state.labBusy?'Running…':'▶ Run & check'}</button><button class="btn btn-secondary" data-action="stop-lab" ${!state.labBusy?'disabled':''}>Stop</button><button class="btn btn-secondary" data-action="lab-hint" ${state.labBusy?'disabled':''}>Show a hint</button><button class="btn btn-ghost" data-action="copy-lab">Copy code</button></div>${state.labOutput?`<div class="lab-results"><h3 style="font-size:14px">Console & automated review</h3>${state.labOutput.error?`<div class="feedback error">${esc(state.labOutput.error)}</div>`:''}${state.labOutput.message?`<div class="feedback ${state.labOutput.success?'success':''}">${esc(state.labOutput.message)}</div>`:''}${state.labOutput.table?resultTable(state.labOutput.table):''}${state.labOutput.output?`<pre class="output-pre">${esc(state.labOutput.output)}</pre>`:''}</div>`:`<div class="lab-results"><p class="muted" style="font-size:11px">Run code to see output, detect mistakes and check it against this challenge. The basic lab can be fooled by hardcoding outputs; advanced Python exercises run assertion tests.</p></div>`}</div></div></div><p class="footnote">The SQL and Python environments load locally hosted open-source WebAssembly runtimes on first use. The full build includes these files; initial loading may take longer. Code execution happens inside browser workers, not your Vercel backend. SQL is a synthetic demo; Python labs use the bundled standard library; additional packages require separate installation and may require internet access.</p>`}
function resultTable(results){if(!results||!results.length)return '<p class="muted">Query returned no tabular results.</p>';let r=results[0];return `<div class="results-table"><table><thead><tr>${r.columns.map(c=>`<th>${esc(c)}</th>`).join('')}</tr></thead><tbody>${r.values.slice(0,25).map(row=>`<tr>${row.map(v=>`<td>${esc(v===null?'NULL':v)}</td>`).join('')}</tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table></div><p class="muted" style="font-size:10px">Showing up to 25 of ${r.values.length} rows returned (queries over 200 rows are rejected).</p>`}
function practice(){if(!state.exam.length){state.exam=Array.from({length:LESSONS.length},(_,i)=>i).sort(()=>Math.random()-.5).slice(0,10);state.examPicks={};state.examDone=false}const picks=state.examPicks,correct=state.exam.filter((id,k)=>picks[k]===LESSONS[id].quiz.correct).length;return `<div class="section-kicker">ASSESSMENT CENTER</div><h1 class="page-title">10 questions. Real explanations.</h1><p class="page-description">A cross-topic exam samples the textbook. After submitting, study every incorrect answer and revisit the original lesson. These are mastery checks, not accredited qualifications.</p><div class="space-between"><span class="chip">${Object.keys(picks).length} / 10 answered</span><button class="btn btn-secondary" data-action="new-exam">Generate a new exam ↻</button></div><div class="mt">${state.exam.map((id,k)=>{let l=LESSONS[id],q=l.quiz;return `<div class="exam-card"><div class="exam-number">QUESTION ${k+1} / 10 · ${esc(getModule(l.module).name)}</div><h3>${esc(q.q)}</h3><div class="quiz-options">${q.options.map((o,i)=>`<button class="quiz-option ${picks[k]===i?'selected':''}" data-action="exam-pick" data-q="${k}" data-index="${i}" ${state.examDone?'disabled':''}><span class="option-letter">${'ABCD'[i]}</span>${esc(o)}</button>`).join('')}</div>${state.examDone?`<div class="feedback ${picks[k]===q.correct?'success':'error'}">${picks[k]===q.correct?'Correct.':'Not yet. Correct answer: '+q.options[q.correct]+'.'} ${q.why} <button class="minor-link" data-route="lesson/${l.id}">Review this lesson →</button></div>`:''}</div>`}).join('')}</div><div class="notice">${state.examDone?`Exam complete: ${correct}/10 (${correct*10}%). Review the explanations before retrying.`:'Submit after all 10 questions to get an exact score and specific correction for each mistake.'}<div class="row mt"><button class="btn btn-primary" data-action="exam-submit" ${state.examDone?'disabled':''}>${state.examDone?'Results shown':'Grade my exam'}</button></div></div>`}
function portfolio(){return `<div class="section-kicker">BUILD REAL PROOF · CROSS-INDUSTRY CAPSTONES</div><h1 class="page-title">Seven portfolio engineering projects.</h1><p class="page-description">Three semiconductor-focused foundations plus healthcare, fintech, data infrastructure and energy/logistics projects. These are detailed project briefs, NOT finished portfolio projects. Complete them independently and get an external review.</p><div class="portfolio-grid">${PROJECT_SPECS.map((p,i)=>{let n=checklist.filter((_,j)=>state.projects[i+':'+j]).length;return `<div class="project-card"><div class="tag">${esc(p.tag)}</div><h3>${esc(p.title)}</h3><p>${esc(p.business)}</p><span class="chip">${esc(p.roles)}</span><div class="divider"></div>${checklist.map((t,j)=>`<label class="project-check"><input type="checkbox" data-action="project-check" data-key="${i+':'+j}" ${state.projects[i+':'+j]?'checked':''}/><span>${esc(t)}</span></label>`).join('')}<div class="project-progress">${n}/8 self-checked deliverables · ${percent(n,8)}%</div><div class="metric-bar mt"><span style="width:${percent(n,8)}%"></span></div><button class="btn btn-secondary mt" data-route="project/${p.id}">Read 8-stage project specification →</button></div>`}).join('')}</div><div class="notice mt">Project completion checkboxes are self-reported. Employers may require years of experience, technical interviews, language skills and deployed-work proof regardless of course completion.</div>`}
function projectView(id){const p=PROJECT_SPECS.find(x=>x.id===id);if(!p)return notFound();return `<div class="reader-header"><button class="back-link" data-route="portfolio">← All projects</button><span class="chapter-tag">${esc(p.tag)}</span></div><div class="content-panel"><div class="section-kicker">CAPSTONE SPECIFICATION · 8 ENGINEERING MILESTONES</div><h1 class="reader-headline">${esc(p.title)}</h1><p class="page-description">${esc(p.business)}</p><p class="prose"><strong>Target roles:</strong> ${esc(p.roles)}</p><div class="notice"><b>Data source:</b> ${esc(p.data)}<br><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="${esc(safeUrl(p.reference))}">Check reference and access/licensing ↗</a></div><h2 class="mt">System architecture</h2><div class="prose">${esc(p.architecture)}</div></div><div class="content-panel"><h2>Eight practical engineering milestones</h2>${p.tasks.map(([name,task,accept],i)=>`<div class="guide-step"><div class="step-marker">${i+1}</div><div><h3>${esc(name)}</h3><p>${esc(task)}</p><div class="notice"><b>Accept when:</b> ${esc(accept)}</div><label class="step-check mt"><input type="checkbox" data-action="project-check" data-key="${PROJECT_SPECS.indexOf(p)+':'+i}" ${state.projects[PROJECT_SPECS.indexOf(p)+':'+i]?'checked':''}/> Mark this milestone personally complete (not verified)</label></div></div>`).join('')}</div><div class="content-panel"><h2>Interview questions and failure modes</h2><p class="prose"><b>Prepare to defend:</b> ${esc(p.interview)}</p><div class="callout warn"><div class="callout-title">WHAT AN EMPLOYER WILL CHECK</div><p>${esc(p.pitfalls)}</p></div><div class="row mt"><button class="btn btn-primary" data-route="interview">Open senior interview simulator →</button><button class="btn btn-secondary" data-route="pro">Review professional readiness →</button></div></div>`}
function career(){return `<div class="section-kicker">KAOHSIUNG ONLY · CAREER LAUNCH</div><h1 class="page-title">Turn your learning into role-specific evidence.</h1><p class="page-description">Target verified positions in Kaohsiung, distinguish AI software / CIM / data engineering roles, practice bilingual terms and connect each requirement to a demonstrable project.</p><div class="notice warn">Job postings change. Never assume TSMC, ASE or Foxconn has an active opening for a specific degree, team or city without checking the current listing. This site does not submit applications or guarantee employment.</div><div class="section-head"><h2>Career resources</h2></div><div class="module-grid"><div class="module-card" data-route="lesson/career-1"><div class="module-top"><span class="module-symbol" style="--module-color:#92d8b6">01</span><span class="module-count">JOB FIT</span></div><h3>Role targeting & location validation</h3><p>Distinguish data engineering, CIM, yield analytics and software ML roles. Build a requirement-to-evidence map.</p><span class="rail-link">Open training →</span></div><div class="module-card" data-route="lesson/career-3"><div class="module-top"><span class="module-symbol">02</span><span class="module-count">INTERVIEWS</span></div><h3>Technical interview defense</h3><p>Practice SQL, model evaluation, manufacturing reasoning, debugging and explaining tradeoffs.</p><span class="rail-link">Open training →</span></div><div class="module-card" data-route="glossary"><div class="module-top"><span class="module-symbol">文</span><span class="module-count">LANGUAGE</span></div><h3>Manufacturing Mandarin</h3><p>Practical Chinese vocabulary for yield, tools, defects, process, data and ML in Kaohsiung teams.</p><span class="rail-link">Review glossary →</span></div></div><div class="section-head"><h2>Local role search · official / public listings</h2></div><div class="row"><a class="btn btn-secondary" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://careers.tsmc.com/">TSMC careers ↗</a><a class="btn btn-secondary" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.104.com.tw/company/yxcvx7k">ASE on 104 ↗</a><a class="btn btn-secondary" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.104.com.tw/jobs/search/?area=6001016000&keyword=AI%20Python">Kaohsiung AI / Python jobs ↗</a></div><div class="section-head"><h2>Personal application tracker · fixed base and worksite</h2><span class="muted" style="font-size:11px">Saved only in this browser</span></div><form class="tracker-form" id="job-form"><input class="input-field" name="employer" placeholder="Employer / team" required maxlength="90"/><input class="input-field" name="role" placeholder="Exact role title" required maxlength="110"/><input class="input-field" name="link" placeholder="Job URL (optional)" maxlength="400"/><input class="input-field" type="number" name="base" placeholder="Monthly BASE NT$ (if confirmed)" min="1" max="5000000"/><select class="input-field" name="location"><option value="unknown">Worksite unverified</option><option value="kaohsiung">Confirmed Kaohsiung</option><option value="other">Outside Kaohsiung</option></select><button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Add job</button></form><div class="tracker-list">${state.jobs.length?state.jobs.map((j,i)=>`<div class="tracker-item"><div><strong>${esc(j.employer)} · ${esc(j.role)}</strong><p>${jobStatus(j)} · ${j.base?"NT$"+Number(j.base).toLocaleString("en-US")+" monthly BASE (user-entered)":"Monthly base unknown"} · ${j.location==="kaohsiung"?"Kaohsiung marked confirmed":j.location==="other"?"Outside Kaohsiung":"Worksite unverified"}. Verify against the official written posting/offer.</p>${safeUrl(j.link)?`<a href="${esc(safeUrl(j.link))}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="reference-link">Open job posting ↗</a>`:''}</div><button class="btn btn-ghost" data-action="remove-job" data-index="${i}">Remove</button></div>`).join(''):'<div class="empty">Add roles you have actually found. Match each posting to your GitHub evidence.</div>'}</div>`}
